{
"from": 209,
"to": 218,
"text": "The L1 / L2 live readings are the only live steps: two `operator` entries and the `hyprctl locked` read before L2, fired by /implement only on the operator's per-chunk word for each (`inputs#I1` item 2); no typed key, no `claude` start, no leg of the round kind (they record files and read no running session's state). `hyprctl version` is a print-and-exit read, no live step. L1 and L2 write `fixtures/hyprland/`, which is committed by design — a recorded fixture set like `viola verify --record`'s `fixtures/claude/`, never a report or a tally — so it is not gitignored. No mutation run (`inputs#I1` item 3): the guards' proof is step 14's `gate.py control`. Every spawning test runs under a kill deadline (`inputs#I1` item 4): the read's own 5 s, nextest's per-test kill. The diff spawns a process and adds a file name test (the fake chosen by its own name), so the hygiene and CI entries stand; the one CI leg is `ubuntu-latest`, where `hyprctl` is absent: no leg witnesses a live compositor, and the replay is CI's reading."
}
],
